  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Sam has ten keys. One of these fits a padlock, but he cannot remember which. He tries the keys in a random order without trying any key twice. Find the expected number of keys he must try, including the correct key.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5.5$ keys.",
      "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of keys tried, including the correct key. The correct key is equally likely to occupy any position in the random order, so $P(X=k)=\\frac{1}{10}$ for $k=1,2,\\ldots,10$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=1\\times\\frac{1}{10}+2\\times\\frac{1}{10}+\\cdots+10\\times\\frac{1}{10}\\\\E(X)&=\\frac{1+2+\\cdots+10}{10}\\\\E(X)&=\\frac{55}{10}\\\\E(X)&=5.5.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe expected number is $5.5$ keys.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
